# Ordered discourse transitions with a written boundary. "Next" by itself can modify a noun or location.
@reader.joiner.and_after_that w.lang.en.joiner text="and after that" kind=sequence cut=yes card_cut=yes
@reader.joiner.comma_after_that w.lang.en.joiner text=", after that" kind=sequence cut=yes card_cut=yes
@reader.joiner.semicolon_after_that w.lang.en.joiner text="; after that" kind=sequence cut=yes card_cut=yes
@reader.joiner.comma_next w.lang.en.joiner text=", next" kind=sequence-boundary cut=yes card_cut=yes
@reader.joiner.semicolon_next w.lang.en.joiner text="; next" kind=sequence-boundary cut=yes card_cut=yes
